  "report_summary": "The post-release anomaly of otel-demo/checkout is a hard failure of order placement, not a latency or availability problem. The release replaced checkout's pod/ReplicaSet while keeping the identical image digest (sha256:5ab0d7b9... on both checkout-f8956c665-4cks7 and checkout-659b547476-vswj4), i.e. a configuration/pod-template change. After it, every observed checkout PlaceOrder span was an error whose description is a downstream payment rejection ('failed to charge card: ... rpc error: code = Unknown desc = Payment request failed. Invalid token. app.loyalty.level=gold', rpc.grpc.status_code=13), and checkout's client Charge calls returned gRPC status 2 (UNKNOWN) instead of 0. payment's own server span grpc.oteldemo.PaymentService/Charge throws 'Payment request failed. Invalid token. app.loyalty.level=gold' at /usr/src/app/charge.js:37:13; payment's pod, image digest, ReplicaSet and readiness never changed. The deepest observed change: payment began calling flagd's ResolveFloat only after the release (0 in every bucket 09:30:42-10:30:42), and flagd's paymentFailure flag impressions - zero for the preceding hour - appear from ~10:31 onward with both the 'off' and '100%' variants, immediately before the Charge errors start. frontend and frontend-proxy show their own 500/status-13 error spans on the same visible parent chain. The exact configuration key that changed in checkout, and the exact attribute that steers payment into the flag-gated failure, cannot be read with the available integrations (no change_history, no pod_logs, no span attributes), so the mechanism is supported but not fully proven.",
